  (note :id note-020
        :context "surface:workstation-config"
        :source_line 557
        :chars 1533
        :summary "Dynamic PTY spawn timeouts are projected from workstation-config timeout-policy dynamic-slot-spawn across direct slot orchestration and intent-engine legacy dispatch paths."
        :text "WorkstationRuntimeConfig::dynamic_slot_spawn_timeout_secs is the single V3 projection for dynamic PTY wait_for_idle spawn budgets. slot_orchestrator/cc_controller.rs and llm/gemini_driver.rs use it for ClaudeCode/Gemini dynamic slots. engine/intent_engine/flow_engine.rs now uses the same projection for autopilot flow spawned PTYs and reports the projected timeout in the Chinese failure note. engine/intent_engine/memory_scheduler.rs uses the same projection for the legacy memory slot path. This closes the old split-brain timeout problem where direct dynamic-slot creation used the V3 timeout-policy dynamic-slot-spawn value while intent-engine legacy lanes still carried a hardcoded 120 second spawn timeout. The intended invariant is: if a worker spawn budget changes, operators edit workstation-config timeout-policy dynamic-slot-spawn once; all ClaudeCode, Gemini, flow-engine, and memory-scheduler PTY spawn paths observe the same projected value; no worker lane is allowed to keep an ad hoc Some(120) or equivalent literal. The code-alignment boundary is intentionally pinned in scripts/check-v3-workstation-config-isomorphism.mjs because this has regressed before through narrow fixes that only covered the slot-orchestrator files. That checker now reads cc_controller.rs, gemini_driver.rs, flow_engine.rs, and memory_scheduler.rs, requires WorkstationRuntimeConfig::load_for_project_root plus dynamic_slot_spawn_timeout_secs at each call site, and forbids timeout_secs: Some(120) plus the old fixed Chinese failure string. This note is evidence-only; the executable SSOT remains missiond-blueprint.lisp workstation-config and timeout-policy dynamic-slot-spawn.")
